<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sino-British Joint Declaration</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1984</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sino-British Joint Declaration was signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> on 19 December 1984 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-thatcher">Margaret Thatcher</a> and Zhao Ziyang. Prompted by the expiry of the New Territories lease in 1997, it provided for the transfer of all of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a> on 1 July 1997, with its capitalist system and way of life to remain unchanged for fifty years under 'one country, two systems'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sino-british-joint-declaration.jpg" alt="Sino-British Joint Declaration" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tomoaki INABA from Brussels, Belgium · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_Hall_of_the_People_%E4%BA%BA%E6%B0%91%E5%A4%A7%E4%BC%9A%E5%A0%82_(Tomoaki_INABA)_-_Flickr.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
